-- title:
--   Definitions for On the existence of bibundles
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *On the existence of bibundles* (arXiv:1102.4388) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `HasLocalSections`: Continuous local sections, with the quotient topologies when used on p.4.
--   - `CrossedModule`: The topological crossed module of pp.3--4, including both standing local-section assumptions. Continuity of the action means joint continuity of evaluation.
--   - `RightAction`: Right action, with the order (xg)k=x(gk), and joint continuity.
--   - `IsRightTorsor`: A nonempty topological principal homogeneous space. The orbit maps must be homeomorphisms, not merely continuous bijections (pp.2--5).
--   - `Bispace`: Definition 2.2 (p.4), with the paper's principal-homogeneous-space convention.
--   - `TypeGroup`: The quotient H/t(G) in p.4, with its quotient topology. Only its underlying coset space is needed by the statements below.
--   - `typeProjection`: The canonical quotient map H→H/t(G).
--   - `unitType`: The type of the trivial bispace; represented by the identity of H.
--   - `bispaceType`: The type of a bispace (p.4). Equivariance and the torsor property make this independent of the chosen point.
--   - `inducedLeft`: Formula (2.1), p.4. This constructs the left action from psi and alpha.
--   - `IsInducedGBispace`: The G-bispace axioms with the specified structure map alpha∘psi (pp.2--4).
--   - `BispaceIso`: Topological, right equivariant, structure-preserving isomorphism, Definition 2.5, p.5. In particular the typed equation is chi∘f=psi.
--   - `unitLevel`: The actual unit-level subset (2.2), p.7; it is allowed to be empty.
--   - `IsReduction`: Reduction of Definition 2.2 (p.7): a single nonempty K-orbit whose structure map lands in L. Continuity and freeness are inherited from X.
--   - `IsCrossedSubmodule`: The crossed-submodule conditions of p.7. 'Fix G0' is setwise invariance.
--   - `OrbitSpace`: Orbit quotient by K with its quotient topology. Quot imposes the equivalence relation generated by y=xk, which is already an orbit relation.
--   - `orbitClass`: Canonical orbit-quotient map.
--   - `ExtensionSpace`: The quotient used for extension in p.7, before any claim that a reduction reconstructs the original space. Its relation is (x,g)k=(xk,k⁻¹g).
--   - `extensionClass`: The canonical representative [x,g] in an extension quotient.
--   - `RightUnitTensor`: X⊗T: the balanced quotient with T=G and its ordinary left action (p.6).
--   - `LeftUnitTensor`: T⊗X: the balanced quotient using the constructed left action on X (p.6).
--   - `DualTensor`: X⊗X*: the left action on the dual is g·y=yg⁻¹, so the balanced relation is the diagonal right action (x,y)k=(xk,yk), p.6.
--   - `PrincipalBundle`: Locally trivial right principal G-bundle, Definition 3.1, p.9. Charts are homeomorphisms over the base and intertwine the action with right multiplication. No inhabited-base assumption is imposed.
--   - `Bibundle`: An (H,G) bibundle is a locally trivial principal bundle with a continuous right equivariant structure map; its fibres are automatically nonempty torsors.
--   - `HasUnitType`: Bibundle type expressed without a point-choice on each fibre. This is the actual descended type condition, not a free map supplied as a new hypothesis.
--   - `IsTrivialBibundle`: Triviality as an isomorphism to M×G with structure map t on the second coordinate (p.10), rather than triviality of the underlying G-bundle alone.
--   - `IsTrivialUnitLevel`: Triviality of the unit-level G1-bundle, using an equivariant homeomorphism with M×ker(t). This predicate also applies before unit type is known, without pretending that the level set already is a principal bundle (p.11).
--   - `TypePullback`: The actual pullback of H→H/t(G) along phi, with subspace topology.
--   - `IotaSpace`: Extension Q×ker(t)G of p.11, with relation (q,g)k=(qk,k⁻¹g).
--   - `iotaClass`: The point [q,g] of the actual extension ι(Q).
--   - `PrincipalIsomorphic`: Ordinary principal-bundle isomorphism over the given base.
--   - `IotaIsomorphic`: Isomorphism of the actual extensions ι(Q), ι(R), with projection, structure map and right action specified on all representatives. Quotient surjectivity makes these precisely the usual bibundle-isomorphism conditions.
--   - `IotaToBibundleIsomorphic`: Isomorphism from the actual extension ι(Q) to B, p.11.
--   - `PrincipalHom`: Continuous equivariant principal-bundle morphism over M, p.9.
--   - `iotaHom`: The actual extension on morphisms, [q,g]↦[f(q),g], from (3.2), p.12.
--   - `IsTrivialPrincipal`: Ordinary triviality of a principal bundle, with no structure map involved.
--   - `IsTrivialIota`: Bibundle triviality of the specific extension: the projection, right action, and structure map t(g) are all tested on its representatives.
--   - `LocalCocycleData`: The full cocycle extraction data of Note 3.2, pp.13--14. Sections and transition functions, with their continuity, are conclusions of extraction. Sections are defined on subspaces, so the empty base and empty intersections require no arbitrary total-function values.
--   - `PullbackSpace`: The actual pullback total space along f, with the subspace topology.
--   - `PullbacksIsomorphic`: Bibundle isomorphism of two concrete pullbacks. Equivariance is tested on all valid representatives, so no unproved pullback constructor is assumed.
-- source:
--   On the existence of bibundles, arXiv:1102.4388v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.4388v2

import Mathlib

/-!
Statements from Murray--Roberts--Stevenson, arXiv:1102.4388v2.
All constructions in this file are local to this paper. Quotients have quotient
topologies. In particular the image structure group is G/ker(t), as on p.7,
rather than an independently imposed subspace topology on the image in H.
-/

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intakethird100.P93

universe u

/-- Continuous local sections, with the quotient topologies when used on p.4. -/
def HasLocalSections {A B : Type u} [TopologicalSpace A] [TopologicalSpace B]
    (f : A → B) : Prop :=
  ∀ b : B, ∃ U : Set B, IsOpen U ∧ b ∈ U ∧
    ∃ s : C(U, A), ∀ z : U, f (s z) = z.val

/-- The topological crossed module of pp.3--4, including both standing local-section
assumptions. Continuity of the action means joint continuity of evaluation. -/
structure CrossedModule (G H : Type u) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]
    [IsTopologicalGroup G] [Group H] [TopologicalSpace H] [IsTopologicalGroup H] where
  t : G →* H
  continuous_t : Continuous t
  alpha : H →* MulAut G
  continuous_alpha : Continuous (fun z : H × G => alpha z.1 z.2)
  boundary_action : ∀ h g, t (alpha h g) = h * t g * h⁻¹
  peiffer : ∀ g k, alpha (t g) k = g * k * g⁻¹
  kernel_sections : HasLocalSections (QuotientGroup.mk : G → G ⧸ t.ker)
  image_sections : HasLocalSections (QuotientGroup.mk : H → H ⧸ t.range)

variable {G H : Type u} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]
  [Group H] [TopologicalSpace H] [IsTopologicalGroup H]

/-- Right action, with the order (xg)k=x(gk), and joint continuity. -/
structure RightAction (G X : Type u) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]
    [TopologicalSpace X] where
  act : X → G → X
  continuous_act : Continuous (fun z : X × G => act z.1 z.2)
  act_one : ∀ x, act x 1 = x
  act_mul : ∀ x g k, act (act x g) k = act x (g * k)

/-- A nonempty topological principal homogeneous space. The orbit maps must
be homeomorphisms, not merely continuous bijections (pp.2--5). -/
def IsRightTorsor {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (R : RightAction G X) : Prop :=
  Nonempty X ∧ ∀ x : X, ∃ e : G ≃ₜ X, ∀ g : G, e g = R.act x g

/-- Definition 2.2 (p.4), with the paper's principal-homogeneous-space convention. -/
structure Bispace (C : CrossedModule G H) (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] where
  right : RightAction G X
  torsor : IsRightTorsor right
  psi : C(X, H)
  equivariant : ∀ x g, psi (right.act x g) = psi x * C.t g

variable (C : CrossedModule G H)

/-- The quotient H/t(G) in p.4, with its quotient topology. Only its underlying
coset space is needed by the statements below. -/
abbrev TypeGroup := H ⧸ C.t.range

/-- The canonical quotient map H→H/t(G). -/
def typeProjection (h : H) : TypeGroup C := QuotientGroup.mk h

/-- The type of the trivial bispace; represented by the identity of H. -/
def unitType : TypeGroup C := typeProjection C 1

/-- The type of a bispace (p.4). Equivariance and the torsor property make this
independent of the chosen point. -/
noncomputable def bispaceType {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) :
    TypeGroup C := typeProjection C (B.psi (Classical.choice B.torsor.1))

/-- Formula (2.1), p.4. This constructs the left action from psi and alpha. -/
def inducedLeft {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X)
    (g : G) (x : X) : X := B.right.act x ((C.alpha (B.psi x)).symm g)

/-- The G-bispace axioms with the specified structure map alpha∘psi (pp.2--4). -/
def IsInducedGBispace {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) : Prop :=
  IsRightTorsor B.right ∧
  Continuous (fun z : G × X => inducedLeft C B z.1 z.2) ∧
  (∀ x, inducedLeft C B 1 x = x) ∧
  (∀ g k x, inducedLeft C B (g * k) x = inducedLeft C B g (inducedLeft C B k x)) ∧
  (∀ x, ∃ e : G ≃ₜ X, ∀ g, e g = inducedLeft C B g x) ∧
  (∀ g x k, inducedLeft C B g (B.right.act x k) =
    B.right.act (inducedLeft C B g x) k) ∧
  (∀ x g, B.right.act x g = inducedLeft C B (C.alpha (B.psi x) g) x)

/-- Topological, right equivariant, structure-preserving isomorphism, Definition 2.5,
p.5. In particular the typed equation is chi∘f=psi. -/
structure BispaceIso {X Y : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y]
    (B : Bispace C X) (D : Bispace C Y) where
  homeomorph : X ≃ₜ Y
  right_eq : ∀ x g, homeomorph (B.right.act x g) = D.right.act (homeomorph x) g
  psi_eq : ∀ x, D.psi (homeomorph x) = B.psi x

/-- The actual unit-level subset (2.2), p.7; it is allowed to be empty. -/
def unitLevel {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) : Set X :=
  {x | B.psi x = 1}

/-- Reduction of Definition 2.2 (p.7): a single nonempty K-orbit whose
structure map lands in L. Continuity and freeness are inherited from X. -/
def IsReduction {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X)
    (K : Subgroup G) (L : Subgroup H) (S : Set X) : Prop :=
  (∃ x : X, S = {y | ∃ k : K, B.right.act x k.val = y}) ∧
  ∀ x ∈ S, B.psi x ∈ L

/-- The crossed-submodule conditions of p.7. 'Fix G0' is setwise invariance. -/
def IsCrossedSubmodule (K : Subgroup G) (L : Subgroup H) : Prop :=
  (∀ k ∈ K, C.t k ∈ L) ∧ ∀ h ∈ L, ∀ k ∈ K, C.alpha h k ∈ K

/-- Orbit quotient by K with its quotient topology. Quot imposes the equivalence
relation generated by y=xk, which is already an orbit relation. -/
abbrev OrbitSpace {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (R : RightAction G X)
    (K : Subgroup G) := Quot (fun x y : X => ∃ k : K, y = R.act x k.val)

/-- Canonical orbit-quotient map. -/
def orbitClass {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (R : RightAction G X)
    (K : Subgroup G) (x : X) : OrbitSpace R K := Quot.mk _ x

/-- The quotient used for extension in p.7, before any claim that a reduction
reconstructs the original space. Its relation is (x,g)k=(xk,k⁻¹g). -/
abbrev ExtensionSpace {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (R : RightAction G X)
    (K : Subgroup G) (S : Set X) :=
  Quot (fun a b : S × G => ∃ k : K,
    b.1.val = R.act a.1.val k.val ∧ b.2 = k.val⁻¹ * a.2)

/-- The canonical representative [x,g] in an extension quotient. -/
def extensionClass {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (R : RightAction G X)
    (K : Subgroup G) (S : Set X) (x : S) (g : G) : ExtensionSpace R K S :=
  Quot.mk _ (x, g)

/-- X⊗T: the balanced quotient with T=G and its ordinary left action (p.6). -/
abbrev RightUnitTensor {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) :=
  Quot (fun a b : X × G => ∃ k : G,
    b.1 = B.right.act a.1 k ∧ b.2 = k⁻¹ * a.2)

/-- T⊗X: the balanced quotient using the constructed left action on X (p.6). -/
abbrev LeftUnitTensor {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) :=
  Quot (fun a b : G × X => ∃ k : G,
    b.1 = a.1 * k ∧ b.2 = inducedLeft C B k⁻¹ a.2)

/-- X⊗X*: the left action on the dual is g·y=yg⁻¹, so the balanced
relation is the diagonal right action (x,y)k=(xk,yk), p.6. -/
abbrev DualTensor {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) :=
  Quot (fun a b : X × X => ∃ k : G,
    b.1 = B.right.act a.1 k ∧ b.2 = B.right.act a.2 k)

/-- Locally trivial right principal G-bundle, Definition 3.1, p.9. Charts are
homeomorphisms over the base and intertwine the action with right multiplication.
No inhabited-base assumption is imposed. -/
structure PrincipalBundle (G M P : Type u) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]
    [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P] where
  right : RightAction G P
  proj : C(P, M)
  proj_act : ∀ p g, proj (right.act p g) = proj p
  local_trivial : ∀ m : M, ∃ U : Set M, IsOpen U ∧ m ∈ U ∧
    ∃ e : {p : P // proj p ∈ U} ≃ₜ U × G,
      (∀ p, (e p).1.val = proj p.val) ∧
      (∀ (p : {p : P // proj p ∈ U}) (g : G)
        (hp : proj (right.act p.val g) ∈ U),
        e ⟨right.act p.val g, hp⟩ = ((e p).1, (e p).2 * g))

/-- An (H,G) bibundle is a locally trivial principal bundle with a continuous
right equivariant structure map; its fibres are automatically nonempty torsors. -/
structure Bibundle (M P : Type u) [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P] where
  bundle : PrincipalBundle G M P
  psi : C(P, H)
  equivariant : ∀ p g, psi (bundle.right.act p g) = psi p * C.t g

/-- Bibundle type expressed without a point-choice on each fibre. This is the
actual descended type condition, not a free map supplied as a new hypothesis. -/
def HasUnitType {M P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P]
    (B : Bibundle C M P) : Prop :=
  ∀ p : P, typeProjection C (B.psi p) = unitType C

/-- Triviality as an isomorphism to M×G with structure map t on the second
coordinate (p.10), rather than triviality of the underlying G-bundle alone. -/
def IsTrivialBibundle {M P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P]
    (B : Bibundle C M P) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : P ≃ₜ M × G,
    (∀ p, (e p).1 = B.bundle.proj p) ∧
    (∀ p g, e (B.bundle.right.act p g) = ((e p).1, (e p).2 * g)) ∧
    ∀ p, C.t (e p).2 = B.psi p

/-- Triviality of the unit-level G1-bundle, using an equivariant homeomorphism
with M×ker(t). This predicate also applies before unit type is known, without
pretending that the level set already is a principal bundle (p.11). -/
def IsTrivialUnitLevel {M P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P]
    (B : Bibundle C M P) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : {p : P // B.psi p = 1} ≃ₜ M × C.t.ker,
    (∀ p, (e p).1 = B.bundle.proj p.val) ∧
    (∀ (p : {p : P // B.psi p = 1}) (k : C.t.ker)
      (hp : B.psi (B.bundle.right.act p.val k.val) = 1),
      e ⟨B.bundle.right.act p.val k.val, hp⟩ = ((e p).1, (e p).2 * k))

/-- The actual pullback of H→H/t(G) along phi, with subspace topology. -/
abbrev TypePullback {M : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] (phi : C(M, TypeGroup C)) :=
  {z : M × H // phi z.1 = typeProjection C z.2}

/-- Extension Q×ker(t)G of p.11, with relation (q,g)k=(qk,k⁻¹g). -/
abbrev IotaSpace {M Q : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q]
    (R : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M Q) :=
  Quot (fun a b : Q × G => ∃ k : C.t.ker,
    b.1 = R.right.act a.1 k ∧ b.2 = k.val⁻¹ * a.2)

/-- The point [q,g] of the actual extension ι(Q). -/
def iotaClass {M Q : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q]
    (R : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M Q) (q : Q) (g : G) : IotaSpace C R :=
  Quot.mk _ (q, g)

/-- Ordinary principal-bundle isomorphism over the given base. -/
def PrincipalIsomorphic {K M Q R : Type u} [Group K] [TopologicalSpace K]
    [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q] [TopologicalSpace R]
    (B : PrincipalBundle K M Q) (D : PrincipalBundle K M R) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : Q ≃ₜ R, (∀ q, D.proj (e q) = B.proj q) ∧
    ∀ q k, e (B.right.act q k) = D.right.act (e q) k

/-- Isomorphism of the actual extensions ι(Q), ι(R), with projection, structure
map and right action specified on all representatives. Quotient surjectivity makes
these precisely the usual bibundle-isomorphism conditions. -/
def IotaIsomorphic {M Q R : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q]
    [TopologicalSpace R] (B : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M Q)
    (D : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M R) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : IotaSpace C B ≃ₜ IotaSpace C D,
    (∀ q g r k, e (iotaClass C B q g) = iotaClass C D r k →
      B.proj q = D.proj r ∧ C.t g = C.t k) ∧
    (∀ q g r k a, e (iotaClass C B q g) = iotaClass C D r k →
      e (iotaClass C B q (g * a)) = iotaClass C D r (k * a))

/-- Isomorphism from the actual extension ι(Q) to B, p.11. -/
def IotaToBibundleIsomorphic {M Q P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M]
    [TopologicalSpace Q] [TopologicalSpace P] (R : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M Q)
    (B : Bibundle C M P) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : IotaSpace C R ≃ₜ P,
    (∀ q g, B.bundle.proj (e (iotaClass C R q g)) = R.proj q) ∧
    (∀ q g k, e (iotaClass C R q (g * k)) =
      B.bundle.right.act (e (iotaClass C R q g)) k) ∧
    ∀ q g, B.psi (e (iotaClass C R q g)) = C.t g

/-- Continuous equivariant principal-bundle morphism over M, p.9. -/
structure PrincipalHom {K M Q R : Type u} [Group K] [TopologicalSpace K]
    [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q] [TopologicalSpace R]
    (B : PrincipalBundle K M Q) (D : PrincipalBundle K M R) where
  map : C(Q, R)
  over_base : ∀ q, D.proj (map q) = B.proj q
  equivariant : ∀ q k, map (B.right.act q k) = D.right.act (map q) k

/-- The actual extension on morphisms, [q,g]↦[f(q),g], from (3.2), p.12. -/
def iotaHom {M Q R : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q]
    [TopologicalSpace R] (B : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M Q)
    (D : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M R) (f : PrincipalHom B D) :
    IotaSpace C B → IotaSpace C D :=
  Quot.map (fun z : Q × G => (f.map z.1, z.2)) (by
    intro a b h
    rcases h with ⟨k, hk, hg⟩
    refine ⟨k, ?_, hg⟩
    rw [hk, f.equivariant])

/-- Ordinary triviality of a principal bundle, with no structure map involved. -/
def IsTrivialPrincipal {K M P : Type u} [Group K] [TopologicalSpace K]
    [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P] (R : PrincipalBundle K M P) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : P ≃ₜ M × K,
    (∀ p, (e p).1 = R.proj p) ∧
    ∀ p k, e (R.right.act p k) = ((e p).1, (e p).2 * k)

/-- Bibundle triviality of the specific extension: the projection, right action,
and structure map t(g) are all tested on its representatives. -/
def IsTrivialIota {M Q : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace Q]
    (R : PrincipalBundle C.t.ker M Q) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : IotaSpace C R ≃ₜ M × G,
    (∀ q g, (e (iotaClass C R q g)).1 = R.proj q) ∧
    (∀ q g k, e (iotaClass C R q (g * k)) =
      ((e (iotaClass C R q g)).1, (e (iotaClass C R q g)).2 * k)) ∧
    ∀ q g, C.t (e (iotaClass C R q g)).2 = C.t g

/-- The full cocycle extraction data of Note 3.2, pp.13--14. Sections and
transition functions, with their continuity, are conclusions of extraction.
Sections are defined on subspaces, so the empty base and empty intersections
require no arbitrary total-function values. -/
structure LocalCocycleData {M P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace P]
    (B : Bibundle C M P) where
  index : Type u
  opens : index → Set M
  isOpen : ∀ i, IsOpen (opens i)
  covers : ∀ m, ∃ i, m ∈ opens i
  sectionMap : ∀ i, C(opens i, P)
  section_proj : ∀ i x, B.bundle.proj (sectionMap i x) = x.val
  transition : ∀ i j, C({m : M // m ∈ opens i ∧ m ∈ opens j}, G)
  localStructure : ∀ i, C(opens i, H)
  section_transition : ∀ i j (m : M) (hi : m ∈ opens i) (hj : m ∈ opens j),
    sectionMap j ⟨m, hj⟩ =
      B.bundle.right.act (sectionMap i ⟨m, hi⟩) (transition i j ⟨m, hi, hj⟩)
  localStructure_eq : ∀ i x, localStructure i x = B.psi (sectionMap i x)
  cocycle : ∀ i j k (m : M) (hi : m ∈ opens i) (hj : m ∈ opens j)
    (hk : m ∈ opens k),
    transition i j ⟨m, hi, hj⟩ * transition j k ⟨m, hj, hk⟩ =
      transition i k ⟨m, hi, hk⟩
  structure_cocycle : ∀ i j (m : M) (hi : m ∈ opens i) (hj : m ∈ opens j),
    localStructure j ⟨m, hj⟩ =
      localStructure i ⟨m, hi⟩ * C.t (transition i j ⟨m, hi, hj⟩)

/-- The actual pullback total space along f, with the subspace topology. -/
abbrev PullbackSpace {M N P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace N]
    [TopologicalSpace P] (B : Bibundle C N P) (f : C(M, N)) :=
  {z : M × P // f z.1 = B.bundle.proj z.2}

/-- Bibundle isomorphism of two concrete pullbacks. Equivariance is tested on
all valid representatives, so no unproved pullback constructor is assumed. -/
def PullbacksIsomorphic {M N P : Type u} [TopologicalSpace M] [TopologicalSpace N]
    [TopologicalSpace P] (B : Bibundle C N P) (f g : C(M, N)) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : PullbackSpace C B f ≃ₜ PullbackSpace C B g,
    (∀ z, (e z).val.1 = z.val.1) ∧
    (∀ z, B.psi (e z).val.2 = B.psi z.val.2) ∧
    ∀ z k (hz : f z.val.1 = B.bundle.proj (B.bundle.right.act z.val.2 k)),
      (e ⟨(z.val.1, B.bundle.right.act z.val.2 k), hz⟩).val.2 =
        B.bundle.right.act (e z).val.2 k

/-- Sanity: a unit-level set tests precisely psi(x)=1, including at empty sets. -/
example {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) (x : X) :
    x ∈ unitLevel C B ↔ B.psi x = 1 := Iff.rfl

/-- Sanity: the constructed left action at 1 is the identity, without assuming
the conclusion of Lemma 2.3. -/
example {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (B : Bispace C X) (x : X) :
    inducedLeft C B 1 x = x := by
  simp [inducedLeft, B.right.act_one]

/-- Sanity: identity is an actual structure-preserving homeomorphism. -/
